screen that never resolves"}]},{"id":"117539140463859150","url":"https://mastodonapp.uk/@katerberg/117539140463859150","createdAt":"2026-11-01T03:49:10.927Z","contentWarning":"","content":"<p>Watched House on Haunted Hill (1959). Shockingly spooky. I expected more camp, but this one kept it straight all the way through and it had genuinely scary parts. There was also enough cool camera positioning and good shadows that I looked up the director. Price’s best role I think.</p><p><a href=\"https://mastodonapp.uk/tags/MovieReview\" class=\"mention hashtag\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">#<span>MovieReview</span></a></p>","media":[{"id":"117539140369642089","type":"image","url":"https://files.mastodonapp.uk/media_attachments/files/117/539/140/369/642/089/original/2f71c874fa282010.jpg","previewUrl":"https://files.mastodonapp.uk/media_attachments/files/117/539/140/369/642/089/small/2f71c874fa282010.jpg","description":"Vincent Price looking like Vincent Price."}]},{"id":"117538929958612964","url":"https://mastodonapp.uk/@katerberg/117538929958612964","createdAt":"2026-11-01T02:55:38.873Z","contentWarning":"","content":"<p>Watched Attack of the Crab Monster. Nonsensical puppet-based monster flick, it was hard to turn off my brain as much as was required, but in those moments I was able to ignore the bad acting to just enjoy the silliness of the big nuclear crabs.</p><p><a href=\"https://mastodonapp.uk/tags/MovieReview\" class=\"mention hashtag\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">#<span>MovieReview</span></a></p>","media":[{"id":"117538929854304558","type":"image","url":"https://files.mastodonapp.uk/media_attachments/files/117/538/929/854/304/558/original/606ffadeaa1da35e.jpg","previewUrl":"https://files.mastodonapp.uk/media_attachments/files/117/538/929/854/304/558/small/606ffadeaa1da35e.jpg","description":"Big crab puppet"}]},{"id":"117527957492964813","url":"https://mastodonapp.uk/@katerberg/117527957492964813","createdAt":"2026-10-30T04:25:12.331Z","contentWarning":"","content":"<p>Had a 2 hour playtest session tonight for Dot-Man, and it ended up with over 40 notes of things to fix. I guess that’s a good thing, but man, <a href=\"https://mastodonapp.uk/tags/GameDev\" class=\"mention hashtag\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">#<span>GameDev</span></a> feels like running uphill even when you’re getting a lot of great feedback!</p>","media":[]}]},"__N_SSG":true}